title: Campaigning
new-page: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1
max-visits: 36
is-card: true
card-image: img/yunquepsoe.jpg
frequency: 100
tags: party_affairs

= Campaigning

Whether or not we are in an electoral campaign, the party is always trying to broaden its voter base. Who should we focus our campaign efforts on?

- @workers: The urban working class, our traditional support base.
- @middle: The "middle class" of government employees, white-collar workers, artisans, independent businessmen, teachers and other liberal professions.
- @smallholders: The rural workers who own their own land, they are more conservative than their landless counterparts.
- @rural: Rural workers who have no land of their own. They suffer harsh conditions, low wages and stational unemployment, those  who haven't join the anarchists usually votes for us.
- @elites: The old aristocracy, high clergy, big business owners and high-ranking officers.
- @unemployed: The unemployed.
- @catholics: Fervient Catholics, who support the Right-Wing Party.
- @root: We either don't want to or cannot campaign right now.
- @easy_discard

@workers
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: workers_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); workers_psoe -= 2 if unemployed >= 15; workers_psoe -= 2 if unemployed >= 25; workers_psoe += 6*(1-dissent) if wtb_adopted = 1; resources -= 1; workers_psoe += 3*(1-dissent) if nationalization_progress >= 1;

We have increased our campaigning among the workers. [? if unemployed >= 15: The high levels of unemployment make our campaign more difficult. ?][? if wtb_adopted = 1 : Adopting the WTB plan gives us a new rallying point around which to attract workers. ?]

@middle
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: middle_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); middle_psoe -= 4 if socialism <= 49 and peoples_party == 0; resources -= 1; peoples_party_support += 1;

We have increased our campaigning among the middle class. [? if socialism <= 49 and peoples_party == 0: The popular antipathy towards socialism among this group makes our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among the middle class than before. ?]

@smallholders
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: smallholders_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; smallholders_psoe -= 3 if nationalism >= 51 and peoples_party == 0; peoples_party_support += 1

We have increased our campaigning among the smallholders. [? if polarization >= 51 and peoples_party == 0: The high levels of polarization among this group make our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among the middle class than before. ?]

@elites
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: elites_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); resources -= 1

We have increased our campaigning among the elites. They aren't very receptive. 

@rural
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: rural_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); rural_psoe -= 3*(1-dissent) if peoples_party == 0; resources -= 1; peoples_party_support += 1; rural_psoe += 3*(1-dissent) if rural_policy >= 2; rural_psoe += 2 if unemployed >= 7; rural_psoe += 2 if unemployed >= 15

We have increased our campaigning among farmers. [? if peoples_party == 0: We have not historically campaigned much among the farmers, and they do not trust us. ?][? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among farmers than before. ?][? if rural_policy >= 2 : Our rural policies have made it easier for us to build support among farmers. ?] [? if unemployed <= 15: The relatiive low levels of unemployment make our campaign easier with the jornaleros. ?]

@unemployed
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: unemployed_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; unemployed_psoe -= 3 if welfare < 0; unemployed_psoe += 6*(1-dissent) if wtb_adopted = 1; unemployed_psoe += 3*(1-dissent) if welfare >= 2;

We have increased our campaigning among the unemployed. [? if welfare < 0: The welfare cuts and resultant poverty make our campaign more difficult, since we are associated with the government that enacted these cuts, and our campaign may even backfire. ?][? if wtb_adopted = 1 : Adopting the WTB plan gives us a new rallying point around which to attract support from the unemployed. ?]

@catholics
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
view-if: peoples_party == 1
on-arrival: catholics_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); resources -= 1

We have increased our campaigning among Catholics.
